{namespace funwithactivity.components.screenSection}

/**
 * Shared "labelled inset group": an uppercase header label above a
 * rounded, bordered content area. This is the settings-table look
 * funwithactivity.profile.ProfileComponent originated for MEASUREMENTS/
 * DEVELOPER (see the `.screen-section` doc in web-client/css/main.css for
 * the exact visual contract — hairline row separators, rounded corners via
 * overflow:hidden on the group rather than per-row radius), extracted here
 * so Sources and Recommendations can present the same grouped-content look
 * without re-deriving it, and so Profile and the source detail screen stop
 * duplicating the group/header markup between them.
 *
 * `$content` is opaque to this template — a settings-row list (Profile,
 * source detail), a list of `.sources-row` anchors (Sources), or a
 * `<table>` (Recommendations) all work identically, since only the
 * outer group chrome is shared, not any row-level markup.
 *
 * `heading` is typed with a bare question mark rather than string — see
 * the identical note on funwithactivity.components.screenHeader.header
 * for why: this project's vendored Soy compiler emits a goog.isString
 * runtime check for primitively-typed params, and that function no
 * longer exists in the pinned google-closure-library. `content` stays
 * html-typed, matching funwithactivity.layout.base.render's own html
 * content param — that type does not trigger the same check.
 */
{template .section}
  {@param heading: ?}
  {@param content: html}
  <div class="screen-section">
    <div class="screen-section-header">{$heading}</div>
    {$content}
  </div>
{/template}
